presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Linking Words with the Same Consonant Sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Linking is smoothly connecting one word to the next when speaking. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We link the same continuous consonant sounds to join words together and make speaking smooth.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To link from one continuous consonant into the same continuous consonant, the linked consonant sound is extended, or pronounced for a slightly longer amount of time than a normal, single sound. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>/r/ is a continuous consonant. When /r/ is linked into another /r/, it's pronounced for more time than if it is linked to a different sound. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Your_red dress</span> sounds like <span class=\"italic\">Yourrrred dress</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">They are_right here</span> sounds like <span class=\"italic\">They arrrright here</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Below are some examples of linking words with same or similar consonant sounds.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying the linked words below:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Consonant link:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sounds like:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"p-p\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">step parent</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">steparent</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"d-d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">red dish</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">redish</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"k-k\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">speak Korean</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">speakorean</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"s-s\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">less salt</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">lesalt</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"f-f\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">half filled</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">hafilled</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Okay, so I was playing the devil's advocate today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm just generally not that comfortable listing reasons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So how about talking first about the positive aspects of you going back to school?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It will be fun and interesting to learn new things.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Silent Syllables in Which Unstressed Vowels are not Pronounced", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>Syllables are the sound groupings in words. </p>For example:<br/>Ca - na - da<br/>Com - pu - ter<br/>Usually, you pronounce each syllable in a word.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some words in English have syllables which are not pronounced.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some examples are:<br/> vegetable  ----->  veg**table<br/> chocolate -----> choc**late<br/> diamond ------> di**mond<br/> interesting ----> int**res**ting<br/> different -------> diff**rent<br/> restaurant  -----> res**traunt", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying the words above. Clap each time you say a syllable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm just generally not that comfortable listing reasons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It will be interesting!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You need to think about your preferences.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Let's go to a restaurant!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All I've eaten today is chocolate. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make up your mind", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a decision about a certain topic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Discussing my dilemma together will definitely help me make up my mind. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about decision-making.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to improve", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make better or increase the quality of something or someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll improve myself if I go to school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reflect on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "think carefully about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You really need to reflect on the pros and cons of going back to school at this point in your life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ravenous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel extremely hungry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All this thinking is making me ravenous! Let's go to a restaurant!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to squander", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend or use a resource in a wasteful way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not really sure what I want to study so I might squander resources. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to kick off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to begin or start something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I might be able to kick off a new career related to my studies. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, brainstorm and make a list of words that have a silent syllable. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying the words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write an example sentence with each word on your list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, practice reading your sentences aloud. Record yourselves saying the sentences. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to each other and correct each other's pronunciation. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about decision-making.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I brainstorm and write down words with a silent syllable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say words like interesting and different.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I record my pronunciation and correct my partner's pronunciation.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}